 "intro": "The Litana forest, in the land of the Boii Gauls south of the Po, late 216 BC, a few months after Cannae. You are Lucius Postumius Albinus, consul-elect, with 25,000 men.",
 "debrief": "In Livy’s account, the Boii sawed the trees along the road almost through, leaving them standing. When the Roman column was among them, they pushed the outer trees, which brought down the rest on the column. Almost the whole army was destroyed; Postumius was killed, and the Boii covered his skull in gold and used it as a sacred cup. Only a few escaped. Some historians doubt parts of the story, but the disaster was real. The other choices are what-ifs.",
